        Acquisitions gap-fix, Item 4 (2026-08-31, agent-output/design-requirements.md §2 ITEM 4,
        §7 GATE FP-1). Adds ONE new component: "Delayed - 14d in stage", the stalled-deal
        reminder widget, deliberately titled distinctly from the pre-existing "7-Day Stale Deals"
        widget (Q3, design-requirements.md §0.5) - that widget measures NO ACTIVITY IN 7 DAYS
        (Stale_Deals_7Day report, LAST_ACTIVITY-based); this one measures TIME STUCK IN STAGE
        (Delayed_Opportunities report, Days_In_Stage__c-based). Both stay, on purpose.

        🔴 GATE FP-1 - THIS FILE WAS RETRIEVED FROM THE ORG BEFORE THIS EDIT, NOT EDITED FROM THE
        REPO COPY. A dashboard deploy REPLACES the org copy with no version history, and a diff of
        the retrieved copy against the repo's pre-existing (2026-07-15) copy found the org had
        ALREADY DIVERGED from the repo in two ways neither related to this change:
          1. `<owner>` / `<runningUser>` in the ORG were already
             `usman.khan.dpeg@avanzasolutions.com` - a real user, NOT the stale
             `test-aysz9meqvl23@example.com` scratch-org address the repo copy carried. The repo
             file was the STALE one on this point; deploying the pre-existing repo copy as-is
             would have REGRESSED the org back to the broken runningUser. This edit carries the
             org's correct value forward instead of "fixing" a value that was already fixed
             org-side.
          2. Two components (`Deal Stage Pipeline`, `Broker Leaderboard`) carry a
             `<sortLegendValues>false</sortLegendValues>` element the repo copy did not have -
             almost certainly a platform-added default from a prior in-app save. Preserved here
             rather than dropped, since a full-file deploy would otherwise silently remove it.
        Report both findings to the invoking coordinator/devops step rather than silently
        "fixing" the runningUser again - see this build's own handoff.

        Component budget: this dashboard now carries 14 of the platform's 20-component ceiling.
    -->
